      "id": "E-R3-MENU-CONTRACT",
      "kind": "inspection",
      "command_or_method": "Independent source/test crosswalk and direct inspection of the retained WC07 captures and menu-recent-probe-01 second-open, outside-after-short, outside-after-region-change and outside-after-long captures. Reused the existing rust-test-02 execution; no new Rust execution is claimed.",
      "observed_result": "The recent-project replay on binary 39d517bb89494ba73725c4da2e7e7fd8b326f1abd3c38dce21a88a3593e03f86 shows the reopened File menu, then a closed menu with focus on File after a delivered outside click at 2560x1000. Project contents remain unchanged and the application exits naturally with code 0. Existing passing Rust tests cover modal traversal, closing without item execution, activation through existing messages and title semantics. WC07 supplies confirmed 1024/1600/2560 geometry. The three after-images reuse one received sample (183079.303337463, PTS 4191760056); they are not independent later frames or a latency measurement. WC07 counterevidence remains preserved; its cause is undetermined. Scope is AC-02 in the observed local environment, not global product or assistive-technology acceptance.",
      "artifact": "docs/validation/r3-remediation-20261118/root-checks/native-final/menu-diagnostics/recent-entry/result.json",
